2. CLM-v0.1-8B (Contrastive Language Models)
--------------------------------------------

Weights:  https://huggingface.co/Contrastive-LM/CLM-v0.1-8B  (file CLM_v0.1-8B.pt)
Code:     https://github.com/Contrastive-LM/CLM
Licence:  Apache License, Version 2.0, for the code and for the weights
By:       Jacky Kwok, Hangoo Kang, Tarun Suresh, Jon Saad-Falcon, Marco Pavone, Christopher Ré
          and Azalia Mirhoseini
Cite:     "Contrastive Language Models", 2026, https://contrastive-lm.notion.site

This repository releases two head files on its release page. Both are modified copies of the
CLM-v0.1-8B weights. What was changed:

  S1-Router v0.1  (file s1_router_v0.1.pt, internal run name post_choice_hn_frompost)
    The CLM-v0.1-8B head after further post-training: 400 training steps on listwise choice
    data, where the other options of the same question are the hard negatives. 40% of every
    batch is replay of CLM's published Q&A vectors with their hard negatives.

  S1-Tweaks v0.1  (file s1_tweaks_v0.1.pt, internal run name wise_0.15)
    Weight interpolation with no further training. Every weight tensor of the state head and
    of the action head, and the logit_scale value, is
        0.85 * CLM-v0.1-8B + 0.15 * S1-Router v0.1
    (python -m innovations.interpolate --alpha 0.15).

Nothing else was changed. The architecture and the checkpoint layout (state_head, action_head,
logit_scale, cfg) are CLM's.

Neither file is an official CLM release. The CLM authors have not reviewed or endorsed them.

No CLM weight file is stored in this repository. The code downloads the official file from
Hugging Face when it is needed. pipeline/run_trex.py and pipeline/run_deepswe.py clone the CLM
code at a pinned commit when they run.


3. Used but not included
------------------------

  - Qwen/Qwen3-8B, the frozen backbone. It is not redistributed here. Its model card lists
    Apache 2.0.
  - The published CLM vectors (Contrastive-LM/CLM-v0.1-Pretrain-Nemotron) and hard negatives
    (jackyk02/nemotron_dqa_qwen3_8b_neg_embeddings). They are not redistributed here. The
    Nemotron-derived data is under the NVIDIA Open Data License.
  - The datasets behind the choice training data: PolyAI/banking77, clinc/clinc_oos,
    glaiveai/glaive-function-calling-v2, allenai/ai2_arc, tau/commonsense_qa and cais/mmlu
    (its auxiliary_train set). The label-reading rows are built from the multiple-choice
    questions of the last three. The agent mix used neulab/adp-v2.
  - The datasets behind the held-out choice test: gorilla-llm/Berkeley-Function-Calling-Leaderboard,
    mteb/amazon_massive_intent, DeepPavlov/hwu64,
    bitext/Bitext-customer-support-llm-chatbot-training-dataset, allenai/sciq, allenai/qasc,
    cais/mmlu (its test set) and openlifescienceai/medmcqa.

